{"name":"Maximum Yellow Red","hex":"#f2ba49","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"maximum","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The highest limit.","The greatest value of a set or other mathematical structure, especially the global maximum or a local maximum of a function."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["To the highest degree."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/maximum"},{"term":"yellow","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of sunflower petals and lemons; the color obtained by mixing green and red light, or by subtracting blue from white light; the color evoked by light of wavelength around 580 nm; one of the three primary colors in subtractive color systems.","The middle light in a set of three traffic lights, the lighting of which indicates that drivers should stop short of the intersection if it is safe to do so."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a yellow hue.","Lacking courage."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/yellow"},{"term":"red","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of the setting sun, blood, and strawberries; the color which is evoked by the longest visible wavelengths (between about 625–740 nm), and a primary additive color.","A revolutionary socialist or (most commonly) a Communist;  a Bolshevik, a supporter of the Bolsheviks in the Russian Civil War."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a red hue.","Having an orange-brown or orange-blond colour; ginger."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red"}],"entries":[{"title":"Maximum and minimum","blocks":[{"text":"In mathematical analysis, the maximum and minimum of a function are, respectively, the greatest and least value taken by the function. Known generically as extrema, they may be defined either within a given range or on the entire domain of a function. Pierre de Fermat was one of the first mathematicians to propose a general technique, adequality, for finding the maxima and minima of functions."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/Extrema_example_original.svg/330px-Extrema_example_original.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maximum_and_minimum","wikidata":"Q845060"},{"title":"Yellow","blocks":[{"text":"Yellow is a color between green and orange on the spectrum of light. It is evoked by light with a dominant wavelength of roughly 575–585 nm. It is a primary color in subtractive color systems, used in painting or color printing. In the RGB color model, used to create colors on television and computer screens, yellow is a secondary color made by combining red and green at equal intensity. Carotenoids give the characteristic yellow color to autumn leaves, corn, canaries, daffodils, and lemons, as well as egg yolks, buttercups, and bananas. They absorb light energy and protect plants from photo damage in some cases. Sunlight has a slight yellowish hue when the Sun is near the horizon, due to atmospheric scattering of shorter wavelengths."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Cornwall_Daffodils.jpg/330px-Cornwall_Daffodils.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yellow","wikidata":"Q943"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red","wikidata":"Q3142"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Modell_einer_Peanoschen_Fl%C3%A4che_-Schilling_XLIX%2C_1-.jpg/500px-Modell_einer_Peanoschen_Fl%C3%A4che_-Schilling_XLIX%2C_1-.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Modell_einer_Peanoschen_Fl%C3%A4che_-Schilling_XLIX%2C_1-.jpg/500px-Modell_einer_Peanoschen_Fl%C3%A4che_-Schilling_XLIX%2C_1-.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Peano surface, a counterexample to some criteria of local maxima of the 19th century","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AModell_einer_Peanoschen_Fl%C3%A4che_-Schilling_XLIX%2C_1-.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/MaximumParaboloid.png/500px-MaximumParaboloid.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/MaximumParaboloid.png/500px-MaximumParaboloid.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The global maximum is the point at the top","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMaximumParaboloid.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/95/MaximumCounterexample.png/500px-MaximumCounterexample.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/95/MaximumCounterexample.png/500px-MaximumCounterexample.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Counterexample: The red dot shows a local minimum that is not a global minimum","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMaximumCounterexample.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipe